# TDD Rules

TDD is the **default** for behavior-changing work. If skipped for in-scope work, state the reason explicitly.

## Cycle

1. Failing test first → confirm expected failure
2. Minimal implementation → green
3. Refactor only while green
4. Run relevant verification before claiming done

## In scope

Backend (`apps/api`): controllers, services, guards, validators/pipes, API contracts, business rules, bug fixes.
Frontend (`apps/web`): shared components, key interactions, hooks, stores, `lib/`, route guards, bug fixes.

## Exceptions (no TDD required)

Docs/comments only, pure formatting/rename, minor style-only UI, small tooling config, generated/scaffold files, one-off migration helpers with no stable runtime behavior.

## Test data isolation

- Never truncate/drop/clear whole tables
- Never delete without exact IDs/keys created and recorded by the same test
- No broad cleanup (`like` on title/email, date ranges, flushall/flushdb)
- External state (Redis, files, queues) only if uniquely namespaced by this test
- Prefer create + tracked PK cleanup, transactions, or test-local namespaces

## Design

Prefer small units, explicit I/O, and business logic outside framework/UI glue. Avoid snapshot-only proof for meaningful logic.
